# Copy to .env and fill in. No real values belong in this file.

# Postgres connection string (Neon). Used by Prisma and the engineering-data routes.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# --- Enquiry email (lib/notify.ts) --- OPTIONAL ---
# Every enquiry from /purchase, the Get a Quote modal and the valve inquiry
# forms is saved to the database and listed at /admin/enquiries. That row is
# the record, so an enquiry is never lost when these three are unset.
# Setting them adds an email notification on top; leaving them unset means
# someone must watch /admin/enquiries instead.

# API key for the transactional email provider (Resend: starts with re_).
ENQUIRY_API_KEY=
# Verified sender address, e.g. GM Dalui Website <website@gmdalui.co.in>
ENQUIRY_FROM=
# Who receives enquiries. Comma-separated for more than one inbox.
ENQUIRY_TO=info@gmdalui.co.in

# --- Deployment runbook ---
#
# 0. REQUIRED, before the first deploy: apply pending database migrations, or
#    every enquiry form returns an error because the table does not exist.
#       npx prisma migrate deploy
#    Enquiries then appear at /admin/enquiries (sign in as ADMIN or DEVELOPER).
#    This is the only step that must happen for enquiries to work. Steps 1-6
#    are only needed if you also want an email for each one.
#
# 1. In Resend (https://resend.com), add the domain gmdalui.co.in and add the
#    DNS records it gives you. Wait until Resend shows the domain as Verified.
#    THIS IS THE STEP THAT IS USUALLY MISSED. If ENQUIRY_FROM is on a domain
#    that Resend has not verified, the key is valid, the site looks fine, and
#    every single send is rejected by Resend with a 403. Symptom: the health
#    check below says "configured" but no email arrives.
#    A Gmail/Outlook address can never be ENQUIRY_FROM - only a domain you own.
# 2. In Resend, create an API key (it starts with re_).
# 3. In the hosting dashboard (Vercel) > the project > Settings > Environment
#    Variables, add all three for the Production environment:
#       ENQUIRY_API_KEY = the re_... key
#       ENQUIRY_FROM    = GM Dalui Website <website@gmdalui.co.in>
#       ENQUIRY_TO      = info@gmdalui.co.in
# 4. Redeploy. Environment variables are only picked up by a NEW deployment -
#    saving them changes nothing until you redeploy.
# 5. Confirm: open https://www.gmdalui.co.in/api/health in a browser.
#       "mail":"configured"      -> all three vars are present. Go to step 6.
#       "mail":"not-configured"  -> at least one is missing or you did not
#                                   redeploy. Repeat steps 3 and 4.
# 6. "configured" only means the settings exist, not that mail leaves the
#    building. Finish by sending ONE real enquiry through the Get a Quote form
#    on the live site and checking it lands in the inbox at ENQUIRY_TO (also
#    check spam). If it does not arrive, it is almost certainly step 1.
#    Cross-check against /admin/enquiries: a row there with "Not emailed" is an
#    enquiry that reached us but that nobody was notified about.
#
# --- Secrets ---
# Never commit a real .env. One was committed to this repo before (a Razorpay
# test-mode key pair, in src/components/.env) and the repo is public, so that
# pair must be treated as compromised and rotated. Payment keys belong only in
# the hosting dashboard's environment variables, never in NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars,
# which are compiled into the browser bundle.
